    "durationMs": 130887,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and fully verified end-to-end.\n\n**Implementation** (Spring Boot 3.4.5, Java 21):\n- Added `spring-boot-starter-data-jpa`, PostgreSQL driver, and Flyway to the pom; schema created by `V1__init.sql` migration\n- `DATABASE_URL` (PostgreSQL URL) is parsed into JDBC url/username/password at startup — no hard-coded credentials\n- `LinkController`/`LinkService`/`LinkRepository` implement all five endpoints; clicks increment via an atomic `UPDATE ... clicks + 1` query\n- Codes: 4-20 ASCII letters/digits/hyphens/underscores; generated codes are 8 random chars with uniqueness checks\n- `@RestControllerAdvice` maps malformed JSON, invalid/missing url, and invalid code → 422, duplicate code → 409, unknown code → 404, all with `{\"error\": ...}` bodies\n- `start.sh` runs the pre-built jar; Flyway applies pending migrations during startup before Tomcat accepts requests, serving in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- README includes a \"Running the server\" section\n\n**Verified by testing**: 201 with unchanged URL and `clicks: 0`, 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 for every invalid-input variant, exact `Location` header on 302, exactly-once click counting, ascending list order with `items`/`total`, and full data + click-count survival across a server restart. I confirmed the port answers on the machine's external IP (0.0.0.0 binding). Test rows were truncated afterward and the test server stopped, so `sh start.sh` will boot a clean, ready-to-graded instance."
